Description: Plasma Keyboard as the on-screen keyboard of Fcitx 5
 When Fcitx 5 is KWin's input method (the edition's Japanese, Korean and
 Chinese sessions), `plasma-keyboard --fcitx` is Fcitx 5's keyboard through
 Fcitx 5's own keyboard bridge (fcitx5 src/ui/virtualkeyboard): it starts at
 login, ends at once unless KWin's input method is Fcitx 5 and the setting
 showWithFcitx is on, shows when KWin would show an on-screen keyboard for
 the touched text field (org.kde.kwin.VirtualKeyboard), sends its keys to
 Fcitx 5 as keysyms (ProcessKeyEvent), and shows the preedit, the candidates
 (a touch chooses one) and the input method switch in a bar above the keys.
 Its window is a layer-shell dock at the bottom that never takes the keyboard
 focus. When Fcitx 5 does not answer, it says so and types plain text through
 KWin's fake input. Test: autotests/fcitxbridgetest (stand-ins of KWin and
 Fcitx 5 on a session bus). A session whose input method is Plasma Keyboard
 is unchanged.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos
Origin: vendor, Sparky Stereo OS (row 71), branch order71 of KDE's plasma/plasma-keyboard at v6.7.4
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-25
